{
    "name": "Dual-Rail Regulated Power Supply (+12V / +5V)",
    "description": "A complete linear power supply: a transformer secondary (26Vpk, 50Hz, with realistic winding resistance + reservoir-cap ESR) feeds a full-bridge rectifier (power diodes with charge storage) and a 1000uF reservoir capacitor, then TWO independent zener-referenced NPN pass-transistor regulators produce a +12V rail and a +5V rail into their loads. Run a transient (~250ms) to watch the rails charge and regulate. (Validated on ngspice: stable +12V and +5V rails.)",
    "tags": ["power", "psu", "rectifier", "regulator", "analog", "flagship", "advanced"],
